The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.

Short description
-----------------

diffuse_interface1:

 diffuse-interface problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 constant viscosity
 first-order time integration

diffuse_interface2:

 diffuse-interface problem on a square
 no external flow, homogeneous essential boundary conditions for velocities
 constant viscosity
 first-order time integration
 by changing the initial concentration different problems can be studied
   funcnr = 1 : unstable stratified layers
   funcnr = 2 : retraction of non-circular drop
   funcnr = 3 : spinodal decomposition
   funcnr = 4 : a supercritical and a subcritical nucleus

diffuse_interface3:

 diffuse-interface problem on a square
 no external flow, bi-periodic boundary conditions for velocities,
                   chemical potential and concentration
 constant viscosity
 first-order time integration
 by changing the initial concentration different problems can be studied
   funcnr = 1 : unstable stratified layers
   funcnr = 2 : retraction of non-circular drop
   funcnr = 3 : spinodal decomposition
   funcnr = 4 : a supercritical and a subcritical nucleus

diffuse_interface4:

 diffuse-interface problem in a brick
 no external flow, homogeneous essential boundary conditions for velocities
 constant viscosity
 first-order time integration
 output using vtk
 the initial concentration is such for spinodal decomposition

diffuse_interface5:

 diffuse-interface problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 constant viscosity
 first-order time integration
 Lees Edwards boundary conditions

diffuse_interface6:

 axisymmetric diffuse-interface problem on a square (z,r)
 no external flow, homogeneous essential boundary conditions for velocities
 constant viscosity
 first-order time integration

diffuse_interface7:

 one-dimensional diffuse-interface problem 
 two phase problem 
 no flux boundary conditions
 Note: only Cahn_Hilliard equation (vp element only used as dummy element)

diffuse_interface8:

 diffuse-interface problem on a square
 no external flow, bi-periodic boundary conditions
 & and a time-periodic source term for the momentum equation
 constant viscosity
 first-order time integration
 uses tec_utils for output

diffuse_interface9:

 one-dimensional diffuse-interface problem 
 three phase problem 
 no flux boundary conditions
 Note: only Cahn_Hilliard equation (vp element only used as dummy element)
 Benchmark problem from Kim, Kang and Lowengrub

diffuse_interface10:

 ternary diffuse-interface problem on a square
 no external flow, homogeneous essential boundary conditions for velocities
 constant viscosity
 first-order time integration
 recovery of a ternary drop
 uses tec_utils for output
 
diffuse_interface11:

 diffuse-interface problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 constant viscosity
 first-order time integration
 Spectral elements.
 This problem is similar to diffuse_interface1, but now with spectral elements.

diffuse_interface12:

 diffuse-interface problem on a unit square
 linear Couette flow
 constant viscosity
 second-order time integration
 This examples is similar to diffuse_interface1, but now 2nd order in time.

diffuse_interface13:

  axisymmetric diffuse-interface problem of a droplet on a surface
  Stokes problem with mu grad c term for the surface tension
  constant viscosity
  variable (static) contact angle
  first order time integration
  Newton-Raphson iterations for the non-linear term in the
  Cahn-Hilliard equation

diffuse_interface14:

  axisymmetric diffuse-interface problem of a droplet on a surface
  Stokes problem with mu grad c term for the surface tension
  constant viscosity
  variable (static) contact angle
  second order time integration
  Newton-Raphson iterations for the non-linear term in the
  Cahn-Hilliard equation
  This problem is similar to diffuse_interface13, but now with
  adaptive meshing using Gmsh (triangular elements)
  and second-order time-integration

diffuse_interface15:

  3D diffuse-interface problem of a droplet on a surface
  in a closed cylindrical container
  Stokes problem with mu grad c term for the surface tension
  constant viscosity
  variable (static) contact angle
  second order time integration
  Newton-Raphson iterations for the non-linear term in the
  Cahn-Hilliard equation

diffuse_interface16:

  3D diffuse-interface problem of a droplet on a surface
  in a closed cylindrical container
  Stokes problem with mu grad c term for the surface tension
  constant viscosity
  variable (static) contact angle
  second order time integration
  Newton-Raphson iterations for the non-linear term in the
  Cahn-Hilliard equation

  This problem is similar to diffuse_interface15, but now with
  pardiso as the solver

diffuse_interface17:

  Axisymmetric diffuse-interface problem of a droplet in a hyperbolic 
  flow field
  Stokes problem using the stress form or one of the potential forms for
  the surface tension
  Variable viscosity
  Second order time integration
  Adaptive meshing using Gmsh (triangular elements)
  Newton-Raphson iterations for the non-linear term in the
  Cahn-Hilliard equation

diffuse_interface18:

  Axisymmetric diffuse-interface problem of a droplet in a hyperbolic 
  flow field
  Stokes problem using the stress form or one of the potential forms for
  the surface tension
  Variable viscosity
  Second order time integration
  Adaptive meshing using Gmsh (triangular elements)
  Newton-Raphson iterations for the non-linear term in the
  Cahn-Hilliard equation

  This example is similar to diffuse_interface17, but now the flow and 
  diffuse-interface equations are solved fully-implicit (in one system).

diffuse_interface19:

  Drop between two stratified fluids in a square domain.
  Ternary diffuse-interface model by Boyer and Lapuerta (2006).
  Two different cases depending on the input file.
    input_diffuse_interface19a.txt : three phases are symmetric
    input_diffuse_interface19b.txt : upper fluid is spreading
                                     between drop and lower fluid
  Output to vtk files.

